Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is a subsidiary of Safran Aircraft Engines, based at Brussels Airport (Zaventem & Steenokkerzeel, Belgium), specialized in the inspection, maintenance and repair (MRO) of the advanced LEAP jet engines that power the latest generation of the Airbus A320NEO & Boeing B737MAX narrow body families. The company is a key player in the integrated CFM international MRO network. With more than 75 years of experience, and up to 20 international Part 145 certifications (EASA/ FAA/ CAAC/ …), Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is recognized as a worldwide center of expertise in the air transport industry. More than a 100 airlines, lessors, private aircraft operators and MRO partners have entrusted their engines to our company. We employ over 600 highly skilled, passionate and enthusiastic employees.CFM International is a 50/50 joint company between GE and Safran Aircraft Engines. For more information, visit us on the Web at www.cfmaeroengines.com or follow us on Twitter @CFM_engines.

To strengthen our Finance Department, we are looking for an Accountant:Your role:

• Process supplier invoices, expense claims, and accounting entries.
• Perform account reconciliations and support month-end closing activities.
• Manage banking transactions, payments, and cash reconciliations.
• Coordinate internal audit requests and ensure timely delivery of required documentation.
• Prepare financial, statutory, and Group reporting.
• Analyse accounting discrepancies and collaborate with stakeholders to resolve them.
• Support the administration of the company vehicle fleet in line with company policies.
• Contribute to continuous improvement by monitoring key performance indicators and maintaining high-quality financial data.

Your profile:

• Minimum higher secondary school degree with 2 years of relevant experience;
• Sound knowledge of accounting standards, financial administration and bookkeeping processes.
• Proficient in Belgian accounting standards, basic understanding of Belgian tax systems (VAT, DNA), and IFRS standards;
• Excellent command of MS-Office and SAP;
• Fluent in Dutch, French and English;
• Works in a structured and organized manner;
• Proficient in both independent work and effective team collaboration.
